2013               /DOUBLE SUBSCRIPTING FEATURE PERMITS VARIABLES OF THE FORM:
2014               /X(I,J).  ALGORITHM COMPUTES SINGLE SUBSCRIPT BASED ON THE
2015               /MAXIMUM NUMBER OF ROWS OF A TWO-DIMENSION ARRAY, E.G. THE
2016               /MAXIMUM VALUE OF I.  THIS VALUE MUST BE STORED IN THE
2017               /FIRST "SECRET VARIABLE" (!).  THE FORMULA IS J*!-!+I.  IT
2018               /WILL WORK NO MATTER WHAT THE VALUE OF ! IS, BUT THE SUB-
2019               /SCRIPTS ARE ONLY UNIQUE IF !=MAX(I).
2020               
2021               /WHILE THE NUMBER OF COLUMNS DOES NOT AFFECT THE INDEXING
2022               /IT IS SUGGESTED FOR CONSISTENCY THAT THIS DIMENSION BE
2023               /STORED IN THE SECOND "SECRET VARIABLE" (") SO THAT ALL
2024               /MATRIX ROUTINES CAN USE THESE VARIABLES FOR LOOP INDICES
